/**

\page org_mitk_views_diffusionquantification Diffusion Indices

The diffusion indices view calculates scalar maps of the selected image:
\li <b>Raw diffusion-weighted image:</b> MD, the mean of the apparent diffusion coefficients -ln(S/S0)/b of the diffusion-weighted volumes, and ADC, the fit of S0 exp(-b ADC) to them; S0 is the mean of the positive b=0 values. The MD of a DWI equals the MD of its tensors only for evenly spread directions and mono-exponential decay.
\li <b>Tensor image:</b> FA (fractional anisotropy), RA (relative anisotropy, the standard deviation of the eigenvalues divided by their mean, from 0 to sqrt(2); Basser and Pierpaoli 1996), AD (axial diffusivity), RD (radial diffusivity), MD (mean diffusivity) and 1-(λ2+λ3)/(2*λ1).
\li <b>ODF image</b> (or spherical harmonics image): GFA (generalized fractional anisotropy, Tuch 2004).

Each map is computed in the background: the application stays usable, and the buttons are disabled until the map appears as a new node below the input image.

"Scale Image Values" multiplies every result by the given factor, for example 1000 to show diffusivities in 10^-3 mm²/s; the level window of the result follows the factor.

*/
